Thanks for the quick response.

I totally agree ... I am all for model building, but I can't use stepwiseqtl because I'm focusing on QTL*covariate interactions. I thought about adapting stepwiseqtl to take interactive covariates, but it looked like it would be too tough.

Instead, I'm implementing a custom forwards model selection approach retaining QTL at each step via on permutation-based p-values followed by FDR. At each step, I choose whether to keep a QTL if its LOD score exceeds a GWERk threshold. Sound reasonable?

John

